# ===========================================================================
# results/  --  EVIDENCE TREE, DELIBERATELY TRACKED.  Do not blanket-ignore.
#
# History / why this block exists:
#   Until 2026-10 this file contained
#       results/*.txt
#       results/*.log
#       results/*/
#   The third rule ignored every subdirectory, so ALL experiment logs were kept
#   out of the repository.  A spot check of 43 log paths cited by the SIVP
#   manuscript's Data Integrity Statement found 29 of them absent from a fresh
#   clone -- including the matched-budget control JSONs, the three-seed
#   ablation and AutoAttack logs, the rerun_docB DOC comparison, and the
#   latency / clean-image benchmarks.  The manuscript states that "the exact
#   log file backing every number is listed", so those rules directly
#   contradicted the paper.
#
# Policy: every *.log and *.txt under results/ is evidence and is tracked.
#         Only large, regenerable binary intermediates are excluded.
#         The negations must come after the global "*.log" rule above.
# ===========================================================================
!results/**/*.log
!results/**/*.txt

# Large regenerable binary intermediates.  These are per-sample dump tensors
# holding the raw arrays behind the pilot figures; they are re-created by
# scripts/adaptive_signal_pilot.py, scripts/final_mechanism_verify.py,
# scripts/geometry_extract.py, scripts/objective_experts.py and
# scripts/fpt_signal_extract.py.  The scalar conclusions drawn from them are
# recorded in the adjacent *_manifest.json / *.md files, which ARE tracked.
results/**/*.npz
results/**/*.npy
results/**/*.pt
results/**/*.pth
